# release-files-excluded — git-tracked files that intentionally do NOT ship
# in the release ZIP.
#
# Every file tracked by git must either be listed in release-files (it ships)
# or match a pattern here (it does not). tests/ReleaseFilesConsistencyTest.php
# enforces this, so adding a new file to the repo without classifying it
# fails CI. This prevents the broken-release drift where new runtime files
# were committed but never added to release-files (see issues #667, #233).
#
# Pattern syntax (per line, matched against repo-relative paths):
#   exact/path.txt   literal path
#   dir/**           everything under dir/, recursively
#   *                within a pattern, matches anything except '/'
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# Stale patterns (matching no tracked file) and patterns that match a file
# listed in release-files both fail the test — keep this list precise.

